{"raw": {"https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7883ac9e6b0bdf019e9456955e0ea4": {"title": "Major Gifts Officer", "description": "Major Gifts Officer.  Carlow University is currently accepting applications for our Major Gifts Officer position. The Major Gifts Officer position is responsible for identifying, qualifying, cultivating, soliciting, closing and providing stewardship to individuals, Foundations and Corporations capable of making major gifts to further the mission of Carlow University. Because Carlow is in an exciting chapter\u2014a $100 million Campaign--this is a time for a solid officer to build his/her career further while using all skill sets and being recognized and supported for his/her ability to be creative. Together with the Vice President of Advancement, this gift officer will develop and implement strategies for securing financial Support and will manage a portfolio of prospects while learning as much as possible. A university Culture based on mercy adds to the positive nature of this position. Travel within the Pittsburgh region and to some small extent nationally is required. \u200b Essential Functions: Identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward an assigned portfolio of major gift prospects annually, while continuously expanding and strengthening the portfolio to reach higher levels of fundraising success. Identify and cultivate relationships with corporate leaders capable of making a significant impact on the mission of Carlow University, while building strong partnerships with corporate staff. Meet annual fundraising and prospect activity goals through proposals, substantive prospect moves (including personal visits, phone calls, emails, campus visits, and events), and securing annual financial commitments to the University. Regularly evaluate and strategically manage the major gift prospect portfolio, advancing prospects through the full donor gift cycle and soliciting when appropriate, with the goal of securing five- and six-figure gifts or higher. Collaborate with assigned university departments, faculty, staff, and constituent groups to develop and execute optimal cultivation and solicitation strategies aligned with donor interests and institutional priorities. Ensure stewardship of gifts received through timely and appropriate donor recognition and follow-up communications. Prepare timely written contact reports, proposals, gift illustrations, informational materials, and other documentation necessary to advance cultivation and solicitation efforts. Attend advancement and university events to cultivate, strengthen, and maintain relationships with donors, prospects, and other philanthropic stakeholders. Lead and execute assigned projects as directed by the VP of Advancement & Alumni Engagement, while also contributing to the development of self-initiated projects aligned with professional interests and institutional goals. Demonstrate and reflect a clear understanding of and commitment to the mission and core values of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy, both on campus and within the broader community. Support the evolving needs of the Advancement Office by performing additional duties as assigned. Actively pursue professional growth opportunities, building career expertise and assuming increased responsibilities as demonstrated performance and experience warrant. Required experience, skills, knowledge: Bachelor's degree required, Master's preferred Proven experience (minimum 5 years), preferably in higher education and in cultivating, soliciting and closing five-figure gifts or more (transferable work experience may be taken into consideration) Knowledge and experience in working in a non-profit environment. Ability to effectively build, sustain and leverage relationships in a strategic manner, both towards internal and external stakeholders, to advance the objectives of the institution Excellent written and verbal communication skills; exceptional interpersonal communication is a must. Knowledge of IRS, FASB laws, strong alignment with the Donor Bill of Rights and deep understanding of fundraising and solicitation policies, procedures and methodologies. Able to work independently and as part of a team. Demonstrated skill at time management, multi-tasking and project management. Goal and mission oriented; optimistic and positive towards their work, department and colleagues; courteous to other departments that are part of our development initiative including Marketing, Enrollment, Capital Initiatives, Finance, Admissions, Academic Affairs, to Deans of Schools within Carlow. There is a high priority placed on the ability to employ an entrepreneurial spirit to approach problem solving while meeting and exceeding goals department and individual goals. Required Related Experience: 5-7 years of professional work experience; non-profit and higher education preferred Progressive track record of responsibility and gift closure Ability to travel is required; evenings and weekends may be needed Excellent communication skills Strong organizational skills, including the ability to manage multiple projects concurrently and manage priorities Ability and motivation to work in a team-based, goal-oriented environment. Technical knowledge and use of donor database management systems. Experience with Raiser\u2019s Edge database is a plus. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859f9fd3baa001a01c91ce7561e9": {"title": "Vice President for University Advancement and Alumni Engagement", "description": "Vice President for University Advancement and Alumni Engagement.  Vice President for University Advancement & Alumni Engagement Carlow University Carlow University, located in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, seeks an accomplished Vice President for University Advancement & Alumni Engagement to provide strategic leadership at a consequential moment in the University's history. Reporting directly to President Kathy W. Humphrey, PhD, and serving as Carlow's Chief Advancement Officer and a member of the President's Cabinet, the Vice President will lead an enterprise whose impact reaches across the University and extends into the lives of the individuals, families, organizations, and communities Carlow serves. Philanthropic investment helps make possible the programs, partnerships, student opportunities, and community initiatives through which Carlow creates an impact disproportionate to its size \u2013 advancing social mobility, responding to consequential community needs, and extending its Mercy mission well beyond the boundaries of campus. Carlow enters the search with genuine institutional and philanthropic momentum. Enrollment has grown 19.5% since Fall 2020; academic and community partnerships are expanding; and innovative programs responsive to workforce and community needs have strengthened the University's reach and relevance. Intentional work to clarify Carlow's identity and expand external engagement has also increased awareness of who Carlow is, whom it serves, and the impact of its work. Carlow has demonstrated that compelling ideas rooted in mission and responsive to human need can attract significant investment from individuals, foundations, corporations, government, and community partners. Its philanthropic case therefore extends well beyond a traditional alumni-centered fundraising model. Carlow has already demonstrated its philanthropic potential. The next Vice President will build the Advancement enterprise needed to bring greater strategy, discipline, scale, and sustainability to that work. Current vacancies provide meaningful latitude to assess organizational design, align talent and responsibilities with the capabilities Carlow needs, recruit strategically, and strengthen the systems and infrastructure required for increasingly sophisticated fundraising. Importantly, this work must occur while maintaining momentum in relationships, solicitations, campaign priorities, and philanthropic opportunities. The President and Board of Trustees recognize that Carlow's ambitions require corresponding investment and are committed to strengthening the people, technology, and resources necessary to support this work. Central to the role will be a close strategic partnership with President Humphrey, an energetic, externally engaged, and respected leader who is prepared to be an active partner in advancing Carlow's philanthropic priorities. The Vice President will serve as the University's senior Advancement strategist: establishing priorities, determining where presidential, and other leadership, engagement can have the greatest impact, preparing the President for important donor and partner interactions, and driving cultivation and solicitation strategies forward. The Vice President will also engage trustees, academic leaders, and colleagues throughout Carlow, helping evaluate, prioritize, and translate the University's abundance of ideas and aspirations into focused and compelling opportunities for investment. Pittsburgh provides a particularly fertile environment for this work. The region's longstanding culture of philanthropy and its concentration of foundations, healthcare organizations, financial institutions, corporations, nonprofit organizations, civic leaders, entrepreneurs, and other partners create a broad landscape for relationship development. Carlow already has meaningful connections across many of these sectors. Its more than 19,000 living alumni remain an important constituency, particularly in the Pittsburgh region, while representing one part of a much broader universe of prospective supporters and partners. Success will require a leader with both fundraising depth and organizational range: an accomplished fundraiser personally comfortable cultivating, soliciting, and closing gifts at the million-dollar level and above; a strategist capable of establishing priorities within an innovative and entrepreneurial institution; a builder who can create a stronger, more sustainable Advancement enterprise and develop the people within it; and a hands-on, action-oriented executive who can translate strategy into action. Higher education experience may be valuable, but Carlow is equally interested in accomplished nonprofit and mission-driven fundraising leaders who know how to inspire significant investment around purpose and impact. At Carlow, the work feels consequential because it is consequential. Its results are visible in the opportunities created for students, families, professionals, organizations, and communities. This role offers the opportunity to do more than raise money or complete a campaign. The next Vice President will have unusual agency to build something enduring: an Advancement enterprise capable of expanding the resources available to Carlow and, through Carlow, extending the University's impact well into its second century. To view the full Position Prospectus please copy and paste the following URL into a new tab: https://acrobat.adobe.com/id/urn:aaid:sc:US:3ff22220-9615-4dfa-965e-457b10162400 LeadExec is partnering with Carlow University in this national search. For inquiries, nominations, applications, and confidential conversations, please contact: Lisa J. Marks, Founder & CEO Leyla Kayi, Senior Search Consultant 413.335.6936 advancement@leadexec.com This position is open until filled but only applications received by Thursday, October 1, 2026, can be assured full consideration. Applications should include a detailed letter of interest and a current curriculum vitae/resume. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University\u2019s resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. Carlow University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. We strive for a campus that reflects our urban setting and is inclusive of underrepresented groups to enhance our University community. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887a198ed641101990bda318868ba": {"title": "Assistant Coach", "description": "Assistant Coach.  As Assistant Coach, the position will have specific responsibilities assigned by the Director of Athletics and the Head Coach of the program, which includes recruitment of qualified student-athletes, supervision of student athletes, assisting in planning practices and scheduling appropriate competitions under the supervision of the Director of Athletics, and any other responsibilities deemed necessary to complete the job successfully. The Assistant Coach will be responsible for recruitment of traditional students to participate in intercollegiate athletics at the University. The coach is also responsible for participating actively in team recruitment activities, including on and off campus programs, assisting in the development and implementation of marketing/recruiting strategies, and supporting set office policies and procedures. This position requires the ability to handle multiple tasks simultaneously and to work in a high-volume, fast-paced and goal-oriented atmosphere both independently, and as part of a unified team. This position reports to the Head Coach under the supervision of the Director of Athletics and will assist in supervising student athletes, managers, and statisticians. Candidates must have previous Coaching experience (preferably at the collegiate and NCAA III level). ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Each Assistant coach\u2019s responsibilities and expectations include but are not limited to the following: 1. To teach and uphold the mission of Carlow University and the Philosophy of Carlow Athletics and the core values embedded in each. 2. Assist the head coach in Planning, developing and executing a season long plan for the student-athletes on your team. 3. Plan and attend all practices, scrimmages and home and away competitions. 4. Adhere to University and Athletic Department policies both written and those established and considered customary and usual operating procedures, particularly with regard to travel and business policies. 5. Provide and demonstrate positive support to other Department staff, teams, student-athletes, and all other Carlow University personnel. 6. Assist the head coach in Designing and implementing an appropriate preseason, and off-season conditioning program. 7. Successfully recruit quality student-athletes with proven academic achievement and athletics skills 8. Emphasize the academic and athletic balance for each student-athlete & member of your team. 9. Successfully assist head coach in retaining and graduate athletic recruits 10. Successfully manage team dynamics and maintain professional, non-social relationship with student-athletes 11. Regularly communicate with the Director of Athletics, Sports Information Director, Athletic Trainers and Admissions Counselors (both in and out of season) and respond to requests for information in a timely manner. 12. Help manage and maintain equipment and uniform inventories. 13. Represent Carlow University positively at on and off campus events. 14. Attend University events when requested by the Director of Athletics; Attend all department meetings. 15. Adhere to NCAA III, USCAA and AMCC Conference rules; maintain statistics and submit all information, i.e. results, statistics, award nominations (scholar-athlete, all conference, etc.) info in a timely manner 16. Regularly check email, voicemail and campus mailbox and respond as needed in a timely manner. 17. Report injuries and emergencies to appropriate personnel 18. Report any issues with equipment, vans, facilities to the Director of Athletics. 19. Represent the Department of Athletics positively to opponents, officials, fans and other members of the Carlow community. 20. Create and model a positive environment that promotes academic and athletic achievement and enhances the student\u2019s overall intercollegiate athletic experience. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7885a89d930819019db0b1f6e421f2": {"title": "Police Officer", "description": "Police Officer.  Carlow University invites applicants for the full-time Police Officer position. Under the supervision of the Chief of Police, a Police Officer in the Carlow University Campus Police Department patrols assigned areas of property used, owned or occupied by Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy. The primary objective of the Campus Police Officer is to provide a safe and secure environment for all members of the university community by means of an alert and vigilant prevention patrol. In addition, they must be equally concerned with delivery of a wide variety of services consistent with needs of the university, its students, staff, faculty, the Sisters of Mercy, and visitors. This position requires a working knowledge of Pennsylvania law, a strong interpersonal communications aptitude, customer service orientation, and a collaborative interfacing with all Carlow personnel. The incumbent must possess the ability to work independently in prioritizing work and emergency calls, keep accurate records, the ability to problem solve constructively; understand and follow directions as well as give directions; strong attention to detail, the ability to work with a diverse population; and the initiative for self-directed accomplishment is essential. Responsibilities Maintain peace, order, and morality, protect persons and property, prevent crime, and apprehend criminals within Carlow University and Sisters of Mercy areas. Investigate all crime, protect crime scenes, collect and preserve evidence, investigate accidents, unlawful acts, make legal arrests of offenders, and serve warrants and subpoenas when required Prepare required concise reports daily, prepare cases for court, attend hearings when scheduled, and testify before courts and other legally empowered bodies when required. Review reports of investigations and recommend further action as necessary. Be familiar with and enforce Carlow University Rules and Regulations, and procedures of the Department. Perform other duties, functions, and activities as assigned. Demonstrates and reflects an understanding of and commitment to the mission and core values of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy. In the absence of the Chief of Police, the Police Officer will report the Police Sergeant. In absence of the Police Sergeant, the Police will report to the Police Detective. Demonstrate and reflect understanding of and commitment to the mission and core values of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy. The intent of this list of primary duties is to provide a representative summary of the major duties and responsibilities of this job. Incumbents perform other related duties assigned. Specific duties and responsibilities may vary based upon departmental needs. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent combination of training and experience. Act 120 Certification. Act 33/34 and FBI Fingerprint Clearances required, along with other required background checks. Ability to communicate effectively, in person, via telephone, and in writing. Ability to efficiently operate the telephone, two-way radio, email, and related systems. Proven problem-solving skills with ability to make decisions and take initiative to resolve issues. Proven ability to maintain strict confidentiality and to handle sensitive matters using discretion, diplomacy, and good judgment. Strong business ethics. Physical: Must be able to carry out vigorous patrol of the assigned area, being constantly alert to observe those conditions of things that promote criminal activity and other incidents that require police service by answering all calls, disposing of all complaints in a professional manner, and recording such actions as required by the Department policy. Environmental Conditions: Ability to work outdoors in all climates. Mental: Ability to pay close attention to detail, to work under pressure, to deal with constant interruptions, to remain calm and composed when dealing with difficult or irate or emotionally up-set people or situations both in person and over the phone. Other: Requires weekend or evening shifts, as well as holiday shifts, as scheduled. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. The intent of this job description is to provide a representative summary of the major duties and responsibilities performed by incumbents of this job. Incumbents may be requested to perform job related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887a19de07068019e21e0fd631e33": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Social Work", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Social Work.  Carlow University invites qualified applicants to apply for part-time online instructor positions in the Master of Social Work (MSW) and the Bachelor of Social Work (BSW) Programs. Positions are immediately available and may be ongoing in future semesters as needed. Eligible candidates must have online teaching experience and experience with learning management systems. Applicants must have an MSW from a CSWE accredited program and a minimum of two years post MSW practice experience. Successful candidates must demonstrate broad competence in social work instruction that employs current pedagogical approaches and strategies. Preference will be given to candidates who have experience with the Brightspace learning management system, and experience teaching social work courses. The successful candidates must demonstrate and reflect an understanding of and commitment to the mission and core values of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy, and experience working with diverse populations. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until positions are filled. Interested applicants should submit their CVs and cover letters by applying on Carlow University\u2019s employment webpage. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and comply with legal and professional obligations. Successful candidates must be committed to envisioning the future of liberal arts and professional education in a rapidly changing environment; have experience working with diverse populations; actively support Carlow\u2019s commitment to equity, inclusion, and community; and be able to articulate how they will contribute to Carlow University\u2019s Catholic, Mercy mission and values through their teaching, scholarship, and service. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and comply with legal and professional obligations. Carlow University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. We strive for a campus that reflects our urban setting and is inclusive of underrepresented groups to enhance our university community. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887a89f8b9426019f95672cc53d14": {"title": "Faculty - Assistant Professor, Master of Social Work (MSW) Program", "description": "Faculty - Assistant Professor, Master of Social Work (MSW) Program.  Carlow University is currently accepting applications for two full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in the Master of Social Work (MSW) Program. Both are a nine-month academic appointment on the Oakland campus in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. One position may begin in January 2027, and one will begin in August 2027. The primary responsibilities of both positions include teaching graduate social work courses, advising and mentoring students, contributing to course, curriculum, and program development, assessing student learning outcomes, and engaging in scholarship and service consistent with a tenure-track faculty appointment. The ideal candidate will be a scholar-practitioner whose work, teaching, and scholarship are grounded in trauma-informed practice and who is committed to cultural humility, social justice, and the future of liberal arts and professional education in a rapidly changing environment. Preferred candidates will demonstrate the ability to engage students in issues of race, equity, inclusion, and justice and will be able to articulate a clear connection between Carlow University\u2019s Catholic, Mercy mission and their teaching, scholarship, and service. Preferred candidates will have practice experience in macro social work and/or direct practice. Requirements and Qualifications Required: Ph.D. in Social Work or closely related field, or DSW and an MSW degree from a CSWE-accredited program Minimum of two years of full-time post-MSW practice experience Minimum of two years of experience teaching in higher education, including demonstrated experience with online synchronous and asynchronous teaching to diverse populations Ability to use instructional technologies, including a learning management system, Microsoft Office applications, and other tools that support student learning and professional collaboration Experience with interdisciplinary course development, scholarship, and collaboration with university programs and community partners Experience with CSWE national standards and accreditation requirements State social work license, LSW or LCSW Candidates must apply online at: https://www.carlow.edu/about/employment/ by submitting a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three professional references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Carlow University is devoted to a culture of integrity, dignity, and respect for all; a strong commitment to social justice; and ethical, forward-thinking leadership. Successful candidates must be committed to working with diverse populations; actively support Carlow\u2019s commitment to equity, inclusion, and community; and be able to articulate how they will contribute to Carlow University\u2019s Catholic, Mercy mission and values through teaching, scholarship, and service. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887a198ed64110199300a257a228a": {"title": "Adjunct - Nursing", "description": "Adjunct - Nursing.  Carlow University is currently seeking experienced nurses to teach clinical in the BSN program with students in Oakland throughout the summer, fall, and spring semesters. Opportunities in nursing clinical courses include Nursing Care Fundamentals, Mental Health, Obstetrics, Pediatrics, Medical/Surgical, Community Health, and Leadership in Professional Practice. Clinical experiences are conducted in the skills and simulation center on campus, and within Allegheny Health Network, the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center, and various community agencies. Course materials and mentoring will be provided. This position is for in-person instruction. The clinical groups are Monday through Friday - there is no remote option or evening/weekend roles. Ideal candidates are reliable, versatile, and committed to teaching and learning. Candidates must demonstrate and reflect understanding of, and commitment to, the mission and core values of the University and the Sisters of Mercy. Requirements: Active PA RN License. BSN required. MSN enrolled is required if not completed at the time of hire. Three years of recent nursing care experience. Teaching experience preferred. Experience working with electronic health records preferred. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887a1a0f425da01a0fd46b4a33370": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Surgical Technology Program", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Surgical Technology Program.  Carlow University is currently seeking an experienced Certified Surgical Technologist to teach clinical courses in the Associate of Science Degree in Surgical Technology Program. The Part-Time Surgical Technology Adjunct Faculty Member will play a vital role in preparing students for successful careers in the surgical technology field. This position involves teaching and supervising students in clinical settings, ensuring they acquire the practical skills and knowledge needed for graduation and national certification examination. Course materials and mentoring will be provided. Ideal candidates are reliable, versatile, and committed to teaching and learning. Candidates must demonstrate and reflect understanding of, and commitment to, the mission and core values of the University and the Sisters of Mercy. Key Responsibilities: Clinical Instruction: On site supervise and guide students during clinical rotations in various healthcare facilities. Provide hands-on instruction in surgical technology remediation labs, focusing on aseptic techniques, instrumentation, and procedural protocols. Assess student performance and provide constructive feedback to support skill development. Curriculum Implementation: Deliver course content aligned with program outcomes and standards. Utilize various teaching strategies to engage students and address diverse learning styles. Collaborate with the program director to ensure the curriculum meets current industry standards. Student Mentorship and Evaluation: Serve as a mentor to students, fostering their professional growth and confidence. Conduct evaluations of student competencies in remediation lab and clinical settings. Maintain accurate records of student attendance and performance. Program Support: Participate in faculty meetings, professional development, and program improvement initiatives. Ensure compliance with program standards and institutional policies. Communicate effectively with clinical site personnel to maintain positive working relationships. Required Experience/Qualifications: Education: Associate of Science Degree in Surgical Technology is required; Bachelor of Science Degree is preferred. Certification: Current certification as a Certified Surgical Technologist (CST) is required. Experience: Have a minimum of three (3) years of recent clinical operating room experience as a surgical technologist. Have previous teaching, precepting, or instructional experience in a surgical technology program within the past five years is preferred. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887a1a12883b601a1317a24c73c13": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor, Anatomy & Physiology with Cadaveric Dissection", "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Anatomy & Physiology with Cadaveric Dissection.  The Carlow University Physician Assistant Studies Program is a 24-month graduate program in Pittsburgh, PA. Our mission is to provide a transformational education that empowers diverse learners to become compassionate, responsible leaders committed to creating a just and merciful world. Each cohort enrolls about 44 students. Position Summary We are seeking a dedicated adjunct instructor to lead the cadaveric dissection laboratory for graduate-level Anatomy and Physiology. The ideal candidate has substantial hands-on experience with human cadaveric dissection. They should be able to connect structure and function to clinical practice, and should enjoy mentoring future clinicians in a rigorous, collaborative lab setting. Key Responsibilities Deliver instruction in human anatomy and physiology with an emphasis on clinical relevance to PA practice Lead and supervise cadaveric dissection labs, including guiding students through dissection techniques, identifying structures, and correlating findings with clinical presentations Model and enforce professional, respectful conduct toward anatomical donors, and support any donor recognition or memorial activities Ensure lab safety, including proper use of instruments, PPE, and handling of embalmed tissue, in compliance with institutional and OSHA guidelines Prepare and administer assessments, including written exams and practical (tag/identification) exams Collaborate with the course director and program faculty to align content with program learning outcomes and PANCE blueprint topics Coordinate with anatomy lab staff on prosection preparation, specimen care, and lab scheduling as needed Keep accurate grade records and submit grades per institutional deadlines Required Qualifications Graduate degree (master\u2019s or higher) with appropriate graduate education as a physician assistant, physical therapist, nurse practitioner, chiropractor, physician, biomedical scientist, or other healthcare professional, and substantial cadaveric dissection experience Demonstrated experience performing and teaching human cadaveric dissection Strong command of gross anatomy and human physiology at the graduate/professional level Excellent communication and classroom skills Ability to work on-site during scheduled lab hours Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience in a graduate-level health professions program Clinical experience (e.g., licensed PA, physician, or other clinician) that brings applied relevance to instruction Experience preparing prosections and designing laboratory practical exams Experience with learning management systems such as Brightspace and anatomy software such as Anatomage Schedule Fridays from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887aca0abfca001a0d017b22c375b": {"title": "Administrative Assistant II - Physician Assistant Program", "description": "Administrative Assistant II - Physician Assistant Program.  Carlow University\u2019s College of Health and Wellness is seeking a full-time Administrative Assistant II to provide administrative and organizational support for the Physician Assistant Master\u2019s Degree Program. Under general direction, this position provides administrative and organizational support to the Physician Assistant Department Chair, Director of Clinical Education, and faculty. The position requires strong professional administrative skills, interpersonal communication abilities, customer service orientation, sound judgment, attention to detail, and the ability to work collaboratively with University personnel and a diverse population. Cross-training within other College departments is required. All staff in the College of Health and Wellness are expected to be willing and able to provide coverage for other departments when a need arises. Qualifications This position requires: Professional administrative skills and strong interpersonal communication abilities. A customer-service orientation and the ability to collaborate effectively with all University personnel. The ability to exercise sound judgment when establishing priorities and solving problems. Strong attention to detail. Ability to work effectively with a diverse population. Initiative and the ability to work independently toward assigned goals and accomplishments. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality and handle sensitive matters with discretion, diplomacy, and good judgment. Ability to recognize and respond to emergent situations as necessary. Excellent organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Willingness to take initiative in addressing issues and solving problems as they arise. Ability to independently acquire and apply new knowledge and recognize learned experiences as opportunities for professional growth while effectively modeling growth. Ability to follow projects through from beginning to completion. Ability to manage multiple complex projects simultaneously. Understanding of the need for flexible work hours. Ability to adapt to change with little notice. Understanding of and adherence to business ethics. Ability to work collaboratively across University units. Education and Experience Associate degree and/or three to five years of administrative support experience working with senior-level managers. Experience in a higher education environment is preferred. Required Skills & Abilities Microsoft Office and Adobe Proficiency in the Microsoft Office Suite. Adobe Professional experience is recommended. Ability to create, edit, and proofread routine letters, reports, email communications, presentations, spreadsheets, and other documentation. Microsoft Word Ability to create, edit, and format multi-page documents using headers, footers, page numbering, tables of contents, tables, and graphics. Ability to create mail merge documents, including letters and mailing labels. Microsoft Excel Ability to create spreadsheets. Ability to calculate arithmetic formulas. Ability to filter and sort data. Microsoft PowerPoint Ability to create, format, and edit slides and presentations. Ability to insert graphics, sound objects, and HTML links. Microsoft Outlook Ability to create appointments. Ability to establish and coordinate meetings. Ability to track meeting attendance. Ability to attach documents to emails and meetings. Exaat Student Tracking System Ability to utilize the Exaat Student Tracking System. Communication Skills Maintain a professional demeanor in face-to-face, telephone, and email communications. Ability to communicate effectively with a diverse population. Ability to remain calm under pressure and when dealing with challenging situations. Proven ability to maintain strict confidentiality and handle sensitive matters using discretion, diplomacy, and good judgment. Excellent written and spoken English language skills. Ability to efficiently operate telephone, email, and related communication systems. Monitor and post on social media as requested on behalf of the department. Critical Thinking and Problem-Solving Recognize and respond to emergent situations as necessary. Demonstrate excellent organizational skills. Demonstrate proven analytical and problem-solving skills and willingness to take the initiative to address issues and solve problems as they arise. Independently acquire and apply new knowledge and recognize learned experiences as opportunities for professional growth while effectively modeling growth. Additional Requirements and Responsibilities Follow through on projects from beginning to completion. Work effectively on multiple complex projects simultaneously. Understand and accommodate the need for flexible work hours. Adapt to changes with little notice. Demonstrate an understanding of and adherence to business ethics. Work collaboratively across other University units. Order, track, unpack, and maintain inventory of all medical supplies. Manage electronic files and all documents related to accreditation. Provide administrative functions related to the hiring of adjunct faculty. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Under general direction, the Administrative Assistant II will: Provide administrative and organizational support to the Physician Assistant Department Chair, Director of Clinical Education, and faculty. Cross-train within other College departments and provide coverage for other departments when a need arises. Determine ways to increase the efficiency and effectiveness of general office procedures and processes. Screen and direct inbound inquiries and telephone calls. Respond to moderately complex questions, provide information, and direct callers as appropriate. Analyze problems and resolve issues as necessary. Greet visitors and attend to their needs. Interface and communicate across various University units with all levels of internal constituencies, as well as with external contacts, including vendors, clinical site preceptors, and professional agencies. Monitor and track multiple unit accounts with active purchasing activities by maintaining running balances of subaccounts established within the department. Prepare financial reports for the supervisor to support financial decision-making. Prepare moderately complex financial documents using accurate financial coding and documentation as necessary. Collect, compile, and analyze moderately complex data and information. Compose straightforward written descriptions of results. Conduct initial research to gather information for the supervisor regarding topics of interest. Draft and/or prepare reports. Independently make and/or cancel appointments. Update, maintain, and monitor calendars. Schedule meetings, classrooms, and meeting rooms. Arrange the use of outside facilities, when necessary. Review and distribute incoming mail and reroute mail, fax, and copy documents as appropriate to request or initiate action and ensure results. Assess the confidentiality of all information received or requested and respond accordingly. Plan and coordinate meetings and communicate with other units, including Facilities and Food Service, to ensure all resources are prepared and in place for meeting participants. Prepare meeting agendas and take minutes. Train, assign work to, and review the work of student employees. Ensure office management procedures are followed and that unit equipment and supplies are maintained. Back up administrative assistants in other University and College departments as needed and as available. Serve as minute taker for Department and College committees and special meetings. Demonstrate and reflect an understanding of and commitment to the mission, vision, and core values of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Successful candidates must be committed to envisioning the future of liberal arts and professional education in a rapidly changing environment; have experience working with diverse populations; actively support Carlow\u2019s commitment to equity, inclusion, and community; and be able to articulate how they will contribute to Carlow University\u2019s Catholic, Mercy mission and values through their teaching, scholarship, and service. Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its diverse community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a diverse community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859fa064222601a0917747d71306": {"title": "Clinical Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) Program", "description": "Clinical Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) Program.  Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic university in a culturally rich section of Pittsburgh. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, it is one of the 17 member institutions of the Conference for Mercy Higher Education. Carlow is recognized for educating traditional students and adult learners for a lifetime of ethical leadership and service. Email responses to job postings will receive a message confirming receipt. To ensure receipt, utilize your email\u2019s return receipt option when sending information. No phone calls please. Due to the high volume of resumes received, Carlow University cannot respond to inquiries regarding the status of resumes. If we determine that your skills and experience match the position requirements, we will contact you. If you do not hear from us, we encourage you to revisit this page for future opportunities. Carlow University is currently seeking experienced adjunct clinical faculty Family Nurse Practitioners to oversee clinical rotations in the Family Nurse Practitioner Program and Women\u2019s Health Nurse Practitioner Programs. Opportunities in the Masters of Science graduate nursing clinical courses include: NU 7481 Clinical Skills Practicum; NU 746 Chronic and Episodic Management of the Family I-NU 7461Clinical Practicum; NU 747 Chronic and Episodic Management of the Family II-NU 7471 Clinical Practicum; NU 7151 Advanced Practice Role in the Community Clinical; NU 752 Advanced Practice Nursing Women\u2019s Health-NU 7521 Clinical Practicum; NU 751 Advanced Practice Nursing Pediatrics-Clinical Practicum NU 7511. Clinical experiences are conducted in the skills and simulation center on campus during immersion week. Course materials and mentoring will be provided. Ideal candidates are reliable, versatile, and committed to teaching and learning. Candidates must demonstrate and reflect understanding of, and commitment to, the mission and core values of the University and the Sisters of Mercy. Requirements: Multistate RN and APRN license preferred but not required; Active PA CRNP & RN License. Preferred Additional States: Georgia, Utah, Connecticut, Maryland, North Carolina MSN, CRNP, National Certification FNP required. National Certification in Pediatrics & Women\u2019s Health is required. Active clinical practice as a Family Nurse Practitioner, Pediatric Nurse Practitioner, Women\u2019s Health Nurse Practitioner. Primary Care, Pediatric Care, and Women\u2019s Health Care. Experience working with Brightspace learning management system and clinical documentation platforms. Experience mentoring graduate nursing students. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859fa064222601a0a1b3eb7661c9": {"title": "Director, Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Program", "description": "Director, Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Program.  Carlow University is seeking an experienced leader and educator to assume the role of Program Director for the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) Program and to teach in the Nurse Practitioner (NP) core courses. This is a full-time, tenure-track, 11-month position located on the Oakland campus in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Academic rank and salary are commensurate with educational preparation and experience. Job Summary The Program Director serves as the academic and administrative leader of the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) Program, providing oversight for the PMHNP and PMHNP post-master\u2019s certificate offerings. In addition, as a graduate NP faculty member, this role will provide teaching in the Nurse Practitioner core courses. Additional duties of service and scholarship are expected. Essential Functions Work with the Graduate Nursing Chair to set annual program goals and evaluate outcomes. Support the maintenance of and adherence to approval/accrediting bodies' standards specific to the Nursing Program, including Middle States, CCNE, and PA SBON requirements. Participate in accreditation review processes, which include self-studies and interim reports. Contribute to program curriculum reviews. Ensure completion of course materials and book orders. Support the program in assessment activities, ensuring adherence to NONPF and specialty-specific recommendations. Recruit and retain students to meet or exceed established enrollment and achievement goals. Advise and mentor enrolled students. Develop and mentor program faculty. Develop and lead student orientations. Address student concerns. Conduct grade appeals. Work collaboratively with the other graduate program directors and faculty to ensure the delivery of a comprehensive and current curriculum. Address allegations focusing on academic integrity. Consult with the Department Chair regarding the program supply budget to ensure program funds are spent as needed. Function as a change agent and leader to create the preferred future for nursing education and practice and enhance the visibility of nursing and its contributions to the academic community. Pursue continuous quality improvement through ongoing commitment to developing and maintaining role competence. Engage in scholarship as defined by the Boyer Model. Participate in service to the University, profession, and community. Support the work of the Department Chair and NP Program Directors. Perform other duties mutually agreed upon with the Program Director, to whom you will report. Other Non-Essential Functions Other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Education Level Required All candidates must have: A doctorate (DNP, PhD, EdD, or another related degree). A master's degree in nursing. Eligibility for Pennsylvania State Professional Nurse licensure as a certified registered nurse practitioner. Prescriptive authority. National certification as a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP). Minimum Related Experience Required: Three years of academic or related leadership experience. Three years of teaching experience in a PMHNP program or related experience. A minimum of five years of clinical experience in the NP role as a PMHNP, with evidence of current practice. Evidence of or potential for an active program of scholarship/research. Required Licenses/Certifications Candidates must: Be eligible for Pennsylvania State Professional Nurse licensure as a certified registered nurse practitioner. Hold prescriptive authority. Hold national certification as a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP). Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7883ac9efb8722019f04b7fab33389": {"title": "Nursing Skills and Simulation Lab Coordinator", "description": "Nursing Skills and Simulation Lab Coordinator.  Carlow University\u2019s College of Health and Wellness seeks an MSN prepared experienced nurse for a 9-month faculty position to work with the nursing and allied healthcare programs, at our Oakland campus. The Simulation Lab Coordinator supports graduate and undergraduate nursing and the allied healthcare programs in the College of Health and Wellness, by managing, facilitating and advancing clinical education, clinical judgment, and the promotion of safe, high-quality healthcare. The Coordinator serves to support interprofessional development and simulation activities across the college collaborating with faculty, staff, and students to deliver high-quality, evidence-based innovative, interactive learning experiences that align with best practice in accordance with the Society for Simulation in Healthcare Guidelines. Additional responsibilities include oversight of day to day lab operations; maintaining inventory of supplies and resources. The ideal candidate should have prior clinical practice and experience working with nursing students. This is a 9-month faculty position, requiring in-person presence on Carlow\u2019s Oakland campus. Attendance at occasional evening or weekend events will be required during the academic calendar year. Requirements Valid, current, unrestricted Pennsylvania RN License. MSN Degree required. Clearances - ACT 31, 33, 34 and 73 Clearances (FBI Fingerprints, Child Abuse, and PA State Police). Experience working with skills and simulation in nursing education Three to five years recent clinical practice experience working in healthcare settings, and prior experience educating nursing students. Excellent written and verbal communication Excellent time management and organizational skills Preferred Qualifications: Certification in Healthcare Simulation certification Evidence of current relevant ongoing teaching and clinical expertise working with patients across the lifespan. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a diverse community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. The intent of this job description is to provide a representative summary of the major duties and responsibilities performed by incumbents of this job. Incumbents may be requested to perform job related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859fa064222601a091b075e829c2": {"title": "Principal Faculty - Physician Assistant Program", "description": "Principal Faculty - Physician Assistant Program.  Carlow University\u2019s College of Health and Wellness is seeking a full-time 12-month faculty to join our faculty at the Oakland campus located in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. We seek a full-time faculty member to serve as Principal Faculty with expertise in physician assistant practice specific to the learning needs of our graduate Physician Assistant program students. Candidates should have expertise in instruction of physician assistant students and have leadership experience. Academic rank, track, and salary are commensurate with educational preparation and experience. Required Experience/Qualifications for Physician Assistant Candidates: \u2022 Valid Pennsylvania Physician Assistant License and current NCCPA certification \u2022 A minimum of a master\u2019s degree in physician assistant (MPAS); a doctoral degree is preferred. \u2022 A minimum of 5 years of full-time experience as PA. \u2022 A minimum of two (2) years of experience teaching either as an appointed faculty member in a PA Program or as a clinical instructor/ preceptor for students of such programs is recommended. The ideal candidates will have: \u2022 A deep commitment to effective teaching, developing innovative clinical experiences, mentoring students, and interprofessional practice. \u2022 Strong communication skills. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to multi-task and problem solve effectively. \u2022 A strong commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusiveness and actively promote diversity. \u2022 A commitment to professional service within the University and beyond. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Successful candidates must be committed to envisioning the future of liberal arts and professional education in a rapidly changing environment; have experience working with diverse populations; actively support Carlow\u2019s commitment to equity, inclusion, and community; and be able to articulate how they will contribute to Carlow University\u2019s Catholic, Mercy mission and values through their teaching, scholarship, and service. Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its diverse community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a diverse community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859fa064222601a0868d72f00e92": {"title": "Teacher", "description": "Teacher.  Carlow University is currently accepting applications for the full-time Teacher position in our Early Leaning Center. Reporting to the Director of the Early Learning Center, the teacher works collaboratively with co-teachers to manage their classroom. They maintain the safety of the children, implement the daily program, communicate with parents, and provide direction and oversight to student workers in the room. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Treat children with love and respect. Must use positive guidance techniques. Must be able to see, hear, direct, and assess the activity of the children at all times. Must follow all policies and procedures as stated in Employee Handbooks. Plan and implement daily program utilizing DAP theory as outlined by NAEYC and the Creative Curriculum. Maintain daily communication with parents and participate in parent/teacher conferences. Maintain knowledge of and implement the guidelines and standards set by NAEYC and Keystone STARS accreditation. Complete periodic child assessments using the Teaching Strategies: GOLD system for child development, share this information with parents, and participate in conferences with parents about their child\u2019s development as requested. Implement Early Intervention strategies as outlined by relevant support staff. Supervise work study students, field placement students, and volunteers. Maintain a professional manner in the classroom when working with colleagues, parents and children. Maintain and implement knowledge of current state licensing regulations. Maintain a safe and clean environment for the children and other teachers. Continue professional development (required 24 hours per year) and keep abreast of current issues by reading professional journals. Attend meetings and trainings as requested by the Director. Perform any additional duties as assigned by the Director or Executive Director. Complete closing/opening duties as needed. Maintain a consistent work schedule and ethic, arriving on time and working an entire shift. Demonstrate and reflect an understanding of and commitment to the mission and core values of the University and the Sisters of Mercy. MINIMUM EDUCATION LEVEL REQUIRED: CDA, Associates, or bachelor\u2019s degree in ECE or related field and 1 year of related experience. MINIMUM RELATED EXPERIENCE REQUIRED: 1 year experience working with children (experience working specifically with infants and toddlers preferred) REQUIRED LICENSES/CERTIFICATIONS: Must meet all DHS requirements: Current (within one year) Act 33/34 and FBI fingerprint clearances, NSOR clearance, current physical and TB test, two letters of recommendation, Pediatric CPR/First Aid certified. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. The intent of this job description is to provide a representative summary of the major duties and responsibilities performed by incumbents of this job. Incumbents may be requested to perform job related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887a19fd3ba9001a024c859ff64fc": {"title": "Campus Visit Coordinator", "description": "Campus Visit Coordinator.  Carlow University is now accepting applications for our Campus Visit Coordinator role. The Coordinator of Enrollment Events & Campus Visit Experiences provides leadership for the campus visits and events planned or supported by the Office of Admissions. This role manages the logistical and programmatic aspects of on-campus enrollment events, coordinates all individual and group visits to campus, oversees welcome center operations, and supervises student staff. The incumbent is responsible for providing a hospitable environment and experience for prospective undergraduate and graduate students and their guests, collaborating within the admissions team and across the University to ensure the success of these experiences. This position requires in-person work five days per week on Carlow's main campus, with occasional evening and weekend hours. Primary Responsibilities Individual and Group Visits Coordinate individual visits to campus that are personalized to prospective students' needs and interests, which may include tours, class observations, meals, and/or meetings with faculty, staff, coaches, current students, and enrollment representatives. This process includes visit request intake, follow-up conversations, appointment and room scheduling, and itinerary confirmation. Utilize Technolutions Slate CRM to build and monitor visit registrations and appropriate follow-up, ensuring that all survey feedback is monitored and data entry is completed in a timely fashion. Manage all aspects of visits for outside groups (schools, CBOs, etc.), including scheduling, planning, and follow-up. Student Leaders Oversee the recruitment, selection, training, daily management, evaluation, and recognition of student ambassadors/tour guides. Supervise all student employees, including payroll, establishment of their work schedule, coordination of daily tasks or special projects, communication, performance reviews, and regular student staff meetings. Continually seek ways to foster a positive team dynamic, instill a sense of responsibility and accountability, and enhance the student employee experience through intensive training, professional development, and/or other leadership opportunities. Events Plan the agenda and curricular/programmatic aspects of approximately 15 admissions-sponsored programs and events, including session and program development, speaker selection, staffing, budget management, and evaluation/assessment. Coordinate event logistics, which may include, but are not limited to, space reservations and facilities requests, catering, IT needs, registration/nametags, signage, volunteers, etc. Provide support, as appropriate, for New Student Orientations, School Counselor Visit Day, Welcome Weekend, Summer Workshops, off-campus recruitment events, and virtual events. Operational and Administrative Support In conjunction with student employees, staff the reception desk, receive and route inbound telephone calls, and retrieve/manage voicemails. Oversee welcome center operations and coordinate daily visit logistics, including tour guide and staff assignments, refreshments, digital signage entry, escorts between appointments, visit excuse forms, visit packet inventory/assembly, swag, requests for special accommodations, etc. Serve as point person for campus tour requests and mascot appearances from others across the institution (e.g., prospective employees, special guests, alumni, etc.) and externally. Meet individually with prospective students/families on campus and present to large and small groups, as needed. Other Support our CRM Slate with various tasks. Demonstrate and reflect an understanding of, and commitment to, the mission and core values of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy. Exhibit professional behavior at all times as a representative of the institution. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Must feel comfortable with all aspects of traditional customer service. Demonstrated knowledge, experience, and/or training in event planning. Ability to develop and maintain positive relationships with internal and external constituents. A high energy level, strong attention to detail, and outstanding project management skills. Must be able to solve problems, think, and make decisions quickly and independently in a fast-paced environment. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. Experience or ability to recruit, motivate, and supervise student staff. Ability to work within a team, multi-task, take initiative, and function with minimal supervision. Intermediate knowledge of virtual event platforms, social media, and word processing, presentation, and spreadsheet applications. Possession of a valid U.S. driver's license and smartphone. Occasional lifting of 10-20 lbs. required; must be able to stand for extended periods of time; must be able to work some evenings and weekends. This position is not eligible for permanent remote status. Preferred Qualifications 1-3 years of prior experience preferred related to the duties specified. Formal or informal education in student affairs, higher education, communication, marketing, hospitality management, or other related field. Background in college admission, enrollment, student affairs, or school counseling (including as a campus tour guide or student employee). Experience with Technolutions Slate CRM. An understanding of and the ability to articulate the value of a Catholic liberal arts education. An enthusiasm for helping students and families navigate the college search process. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859e9f4435ab019f85968c917ce6": {"title": "Enrollment Counselor (Adult/Graduate Students)", "description": "Enrollment Counselor (Adult/Graduate Students).  Carlow University is currently accepting applications for our Enrollment Counselor (Adult/Graduate Students) position. The Enrollment Counselor will recruit and enroll a talented and diverse class of transfer, adult, and graduate students each year. The incumbent will engage with these students through the entire enrollment process, from inquiry to matriculation, serving as a single point of contact. This includes frequent correspondence, application review, basic financial aid counseling, and ensuring that all requirements are met for a smooth transition to the university. Within a collaborative environment, the Enrollment Counselor will lead or contribute to one or more strategic initiatives, serve as a liaison to one or more campus offices/departments/colleges, and use independent analysis and decision making to develop and execute strategies to increase applications and enrollment of these students. Primary Responsibilities Incorporating data analysis, the incumbent will develop and implement an effective recruitment strategy for the programs and partnerships for which they have been assigned. Responsibilities include: Plans and conducts recruitment presentations at community colleges. Represents the University at college and graduate/career fairs. Employs CRM (Slate) and SIS (Colleague) daily to manage the recruitment funnel and registration process. Uses an established communication flow to qualify inquiries, set appointments, encourage applications, and follow up with applicants, admits, and deposits, with the constant goal of moving students along effectively in the admissions process. Develops effective written, email, or text correspondence to enhance individual program recruitment management. Meets with prospective students during individual campus visits as well as in-person and virtual events. Maintains familiarity with partnership and articulation agreements to promote to students who are looking to transfer to Carlow from specific institutions. Provides information on Carlow's academic programs, admissions process, financial aid, and scholarships to various faculty/staff at other academic institutions or corporate partners within our region. Supports enrollment efforts with corporate partners and serves as an enrollment counselor for students affiliated with our corporate partners. Helps to manage strategic partnerships and/or vendor relationships as needed, including with online program management. Reviews admissions applications and makes admissions decisions on a regular basis. Assists students with various aspects of the financial aid process. Addresses questions regarding the billing process and any other issues that arise during onboarding. Performs necessary follow-up with enrolled students to ensure all onboarding steps are fulfilled and any outstanding requirements/paperwork are received. Aggressively and proactively monitors and adjusts progress toward goals. Nurtures relationships with community college counselors/advisors and other influencers or constituents (e.g., faculty, coaches). Conducts unofficial credit evaluations upon request to provide prospective students with a general sense of how many previously earned college credits will transfer to Carlow as needed. Works closely with the Student Success Coordinator, or other designated individuals, to prioritize and ensure a quick turnaround time for official transfer credit evaluations. Conducts ongoing benchmarking and competitor research, as well as evaluation of trends in higher education, to make recommendations for program or process improvements. Participates in the ongoing development, implementation, and assessment of all recruitment strategies, in line with office processes and procedures. Attends regular strategy discussions, staff meetings, and professional development opportunities. Facilitates international recruitment management when required. Participates in, and may be required to organize, an online enrollment event. Liaison Duties Acts as an intermediary between the Office of Admissions and an assigned college, office, and/or department within Carlow University. Becomes an in-house expert on the programs, procedures, and/or offerings of said college, office, and/or department, and serves as a resource to peers within the Office of Admissions. Attends meetings of the college, office, and/or department as a representative of the Office of Admissions, as appropriate. Other Demonstrates and reflects an understanding of, and commitment to, the mission and core values of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy. Always exhibits professional behavior as a representative of the institution. Performs other duties as assigned to address and develop personal and professional skill areas and interests, as well as to help meet overall office objectives. The level and extent to which these projects/areas are assigned, either as primary or secondary responsibilities, will correspond with the recruiter's experience, skills, and time management abilities. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Excellent customer service, phone, and organizational skills. Ability to work efficiently in a high-volume, fast-paced environment and with diverse populations. Ability to communicate effectively with a variety of constituents by telephone, in writing, and in person. Intermediate level of proficiency with basic computer software systems (i.e., Microsoft Office). Knowledge of, or willingness to learn, financial aid processes. Possession of a valid U.S. driver's license. Ability to work some evenings and weekends. Willingness to travel independently and transport self and an extensive supply of recruitment materials in a timely manner from location to location. Ability to occasionally lift 10-20 lb. boxes. Ability to stand for extended periods of time. Preferred Qualifications Proven sales or admissions experience in a goal-oriented operation. Ability to collect and interpret data to make strategic decisions. An understanding of, and the ability to articulate, the value of a Catholic liberal arts education. Familiarity with SIS and CRM systems is a plus. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859fa064222601a087496eed6bda": {"title": "Enrollment Counselor (First Year Students)", "description": "Enrollment Counselor (First Year Students).  Carlow University is currently accepting applications for our Enrollment Counselor (First Year Students) position. The Enrollment Counselor will recruit and enroll a talented and diverse class of traditional first-year undergraduate students each year. The incumbent will shepherd these students through the entire enrollment process, from inquiry to matriculation, serving as a single point of contact. This includes frequent correspondence, application review, financial aid counseling, and ensuring that all requirements are met for a smooth transition to college. Within a collaborative environment, the Enrollment Counselor may serve as a liaison to one or more campus offices/departments/colleges and will support one or more of the office\u2019s strategic initiatives, such as first-year experience, access and outreach, or enrollment communications. This position is based on Carlow\u2019s main campus and requires some weekend and evening work. Occasional overnight travel is also expected. Primary Responsibilities Recruitment/Territory Management Create a comprehensive plan for travel to, and coverage of, high school visits, college fairs, and regional events by both the incumbent and alumni/parent ambassadors. Plan regional or school-based events, as appropriate, for school counselors, prospective students/families, and admitted students/families. Use Technolutions Slate CRM to maintain consistent communication with prospective students and families with a focus on encouraging applications, campus visits, enrollment deposits, etc. Nurture relationships with school counselors, alumni/parent ambassadors based in the territory, and other influencers and constituents (e.g., teachers, principals, coaches). Assess candidates and make recommendations for admission and merit scholarships. Counsel students and families on financial aid, to include FAFSA completion, release of financial aid offers, and thorough explanation of college costs, loans, and payment options. Assist students with the transition/onboarding process from the time of deposit until start of classes, including satisfactory completion of various tasks and paperwork such as housing, technology setup, financial aid verification, immunization record, etc. Present to large and small groups of prospective students and families on and off campus (enrollment events, high school parent nights, etc.). Use independent analysis and decision making to develop and execute strategies to increase applications and enrollment in the assigned recruitment territory. Strategic Initiatives/Liaison Act as an intermediary between the Office of Admissions and an assigned college, office, and/or department within Carlow University. Lead and/or support a critical strategic initiative, such as: Coordinate aspects of the First-Year Experience, including onboarding communications, First-Year Orientation (summer), and Welcome Weekend (start of fall semester). Develop and implement plans to enhance access and outreach initiatives, including the creation and maintenance of an accurate database of community-based organizations (CBOs) and their leaders/representatives. Establish a communication plan to inform and engage CBOs. Establish, execute, and evaluate a comprehensive multi-channel communication strategy and editorial content calendar that drives prospective undergraduate and graduate students to inquire, apply, visit, and enroll. Serve as lead copywriter and liaison with enrollment-specific marketing partners/vendors. Other Participate actively, as applicable and appropriate, in profession-specific association conferences, webinars, listservs, and volunteer roles to represent Carlow, gain new ideas and insights, and develop professionally. Demonstrate and reflect an understanding of, and commitment to, the mission and core values of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy. Exhibit professional behavior at all times as a representative of the institution. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree required Experience in collegiate student leader in admissions, student government, residence life, or first-year experience OR graduate/professional experience in admissions, enrollment, student affairs, school counseling, or related field A high energy level, strong attention to detail, and outstanding project management skills Excellent oral and written communication skills Strong customer service skills Understanding of, and commitment to, inclusive enrollment practices Ability to multi\u2010task, take initiative, and function with minimal supervision Ability to collect and interpret data to make strategic decisions Possession of a smart phone capable of text messaging as well as a valid U.S. driver\u2019s license. Must be willing to travel independently, including local (same day) travel as well as occasional overnight travel (approximately 2-3 weeks in the fall and 1-2 weeks in the spring); Occasional lifting of 10-20 lb. boxes will be required; Will need to be able to stand for extended periods of time; Must be able to work some evenings and weekends. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree is preferred 1-3 years\u2019 experience in admissions, enrollment, student affairs, school counseling, or related field Demonstrated knowledge, experience, and/or training in event planning Ability to develop and maintain positive relationships with internal and external constituents Familiarity with the work of community-based organizations or similar college access initiatives An understanding of and the ability to articulate the value of a Catholic liberal arts education An enthusiasm for helping students and families navigate the college search process Should have an intermediate level of proficiency with basic computer software systems (i.e. Microsoft Office); Familiarity with SIS and CRM systems is a plus. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887a198ed641101990bd7832a66cd": {"title": "Housekeeper II", "description": "Housekeeper II.  Carlow University is seeking a full-time Housekeeper II. Responsibilities include cleaning and assigned area such as a small building, a portion of a larger building, or a group of offices. Duties require making routine work decisions independently although work usually follows established methods and work procedures. Employees in the class may perform duties such as ordering and reordering supplies for the storage space in their assigned area via the \u201cRequest for Supplies\u201d form and distributing supplies to the other Housekeeping employees, reporting needed repairs to a supervisor, and training new employees in the materials, methods, and practices used in cleaning operations. In addition to the normal duties of a Housekeeper I a Housekeeper II will be expected to perform the following: Washes, waxes, dusts, and polishes floors Operates housekeeping equipment including but not limited to floor scrubbers, buffers, burnishers, carpet extractors, etc. Moves furniture and equipment; delivers bulk supplies Provides the set-up and preparation for banquets, special events and special functions. We seek individuals with the following qualifications: High school graduate or GED. Knowledge of OSHA regulations for chemicals and materials used in housekeeping operations Four years previous institutional housekeeping experience. Ability to communicate effectively in person is essential. Ability to walk or stand 95% of the time is required. Valid PA Driver's License is required. Applicant must complete a criminal background check, physical examination, and drug test. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Successful candidates must be committed to envisioning the future of liberal arts and professional education in a rapidly changing environment; have experience working with diverse populations; actively support Carlow\u2019s commitment to equity, inclusion, and community; and be able to articulate how they will contribute to Carlow University\u2019s Catholic, Mercy mission and values through their teaching, scholarship, and service. Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its diverse community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a diverse community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. The intent of this job description is to provide a representative summary of the major duties and responsibilities performed by incumbents of this job. Incumbents may be requested to perform job related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887aca0abfca001a0d924f3860b78": {"title": "Housekeeping Supervisor", "description": "Housekeeping Supervisor.  Carlow University invites applications for a full-time Housekeeping Supervisor. The Housekeeping Supervisor supervises the work activities of Housekeeper 1, 2, and 3 staff to ensure a clean, orderly, and attractive atmosphere throughout the University. The Housekeeping Supervisor assigns duties, inspects work, investigates complaints regarding housekeeping services and equipment, and takes corrective action. The Housekeeping Supervisor purchases housekeeping supplies and equipment, takes inventories as needed, and trains new employees. Responsibilities The Housekeeping Supervisor will: Develop and implement strategies to improve the efficiency of the housekeeping staff. Consult, supervise, and work with staff to improve housekeeping services. Schedule shifts and arrange for replacements in cases of absence. Develop Standard Operating Procedures and Policies with the Facilities Management team. Perform daily housekeeping inspections on all housekeeping staff to verify they are completing their daily job responsibilities. Assist the assigned Housekeeper 3 in charge of inventory to order supplies needed and ensure that the inventory being kept onsite is sufficient. Manage all campus events for housekeeping, including: Create and maintain the events schedule for setups and teardowns. Assign Housekeepers to perform setups and teardowns for each event. Assign and close out all event and general housekeeping work orders to staff. Attend the Events Committee weekly meeting. Work with the Facilities Management team in creating a capital budget for housekeeping equipment. Oversee critical housekeeping initiatives during certain University closures. Assist the cost center owner in creating an operating budget for housekeeping supplies and/or other needs. Train Housekeepers on cleaning and maintenance tasks for Housekeeper 3. Respond to customer complaints and special requests. Participate in large cleaning projects as required. Ensure compliance with safety and sanitation policies in all areas. Work with Facilities Management and Residence Life to coordinate, schedule, and manage all dorm room cleans. Schedule and manage all floor care projects and associated floor care maintenance. Perform or assist with cleaning duties as necessary. Qualifications Carlow University seeks an individual with the following qualifications: High School diploma or GED required. Two or more years of work experience as a Housekeeping Supervisor. Preferred knowledge of supervising in a union environment. Excellent organizational and team management skills. Flexibility to work various shifts, including evenings, weekends, and University Holidays. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Successful candidates must be committed to envisioning the future of liberal arts and professional education in a rapidly changing environment; have experience working with diverse populations; actively support Carlow\u2019s commitment to equity, inclusion, and community; and be able to articulate how they will contribute to Carlow University\u2019s Catholic, Mercy mission and values through their teaching, scholarship, and service. Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its diverse community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a diverse community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887aca0abfca001a0ca82471f7b31": {"title": "Maintenance Mechanic 2", "description": "Maintenance Mechanic 2.  Carlow University is seeking a skilled and dependable Maintenance Mechanic II to join our Facilities team on a full-time basis. In this journey-level, multi-trade position, you will play a critical role in keeping our Pittsburgh campus safe, functional, and welcoming for students, faculty, and staff. This is a hands-on opportunity for an experienced trades professional who takes pride in quality workmanship across carpentry, plumbing, electrical, welding, painting, masonry, and mechanical systems. You will exercise technical independence, lead helpers on assigned tasks, and work directly within the policies, procedures, and mission of Carlow University and the Sisters of Mercy. Job Duties: Repairs doors, door frames, and furniture; fabricates and installs temporary partitions; builds forms; and operates and maintains wood lathe, sanders, jointer, power saw, planer, and related power and hand tools to perform assigned carpentry duties. Paints and decorates interiors of buildings; and performs masonry work in connection with buildings, foundations, walks, and walls. Installs and maintains plumbing fixtures; maintains steam lines, steam heating, and cooking equipment; and measures, cuts, threads and installs pipe for steam and water lines. Installs electric circuits, wall plugs, and lighting fixtures; and repairs and reconditions fans. Makes repairs and adjustments to laundry washing, drying and pressing machinery, and schedules oiling and greasing of equipment. Performs lead work over helpers performing basic assignments. Makes repairs to roofs and installs flashing and spouts. Welds and brazes metals by use of arc and acetylene welders; and erects steel for construction. Performs repair on structures, such as building forms, finishing concrete, welding steel components, and operating construction equipment when required. Removes snow from sidewalks and entryways using basic snow removal equipment. Performs related work as required. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of the methods, materials, tools, and practices used in at least two of the building, electrical, or mechanical trades. Knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trades involved. Ability to care for and use the tools and equipment utilized in the trades involved. Ability to detect defects in equipment and to make proper repairs or adjustments. Ability to lead a small group of semi-skilled workers. Ability to interpret and work from pencil sketches and diagrams. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Ability to operate and/or utilize basic lawn care and snow removal equipment. Ability to lift and move heavy objects and to work under adverse weather conditions. Must be able to walk or stand 95% of the time. Must have valid PA driver\u2019s license. Minimum Experience & Training: Four years of experience in building and plant maintenance work, which has involved at least two of the building, electrical, or mechanical trades or any equivalent combination of experience and training that affords the applicant with the required knowledge, skills, and abilities. Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Successful candidates must be committed to envisioning the future of liberal arts and professional education in a rapidly changing environment; have experience working with diverse populations; actively support Carlow\u2019s commitment to equity, inclusion, and community; and be able to articulate how they will contribute to Carlow University\u2019s Catholic, Mercy mission and values through their teaching, scholarship, and service. Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its diverse community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a diverse community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. The intent of this job description is to provide a representative summary of the major duties and responsibilities performed by incumbents of this job. Incumbents may be requested to perform job related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7885a8a03fc26101a05f6f0f6e3adf": {"title": "Shared Administrative Assistant - Human Resources & Finance", "description": "Shared Administrative Assistant - Human Resources & Finance.  Carlow University seeks an experienced Shared Administrative Assistant - Human Resources and Finance, to provide administrative and operational support to both the Office of Human Resources and Finance and Accounting Office. This role assists with maintaining personnel and financial records, supports payroll administration and processing, and helps ensure compliance with university policies and applicable regulations. The Shared Administrative Assistant - Human Resources and Finance serves as a key resource in coordinating HR and financial functions related to payroll support, board activities, maintaining data accuracy, alongside delivering efficient internal support to employees and management. A core responsibility of this role is attendance at quarterly committee meetings and taking meeting minutes. The meeting minutes must then be reviewed and sent out to committee members on a timely basis with careful attention to deadlines. Key responsibilities include assisting with payroll preparation and processing, maintaining employee payroll records, tracking time and attendance data, processing invoices and financial transactions, reconciling records, supporting benefits administration and preparing reports and presentations, as directed. The position requires strong attention to detail, confidentiality, organizational skills, and the ability to manage multiple priorities while providing excellent customer service to internal and external stakeholders. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Maintain personnel and financial records. \u200bProcess and administer biweekly payroll for all employees, ensuring accuracy and timeliness. Review and verify employee timesheets, attendance records, and payroll data prior to payroll processing. Enter and maintain payroll information, including new hires, terminations, salary changes, deductions, and direct deposit updates. Calculate wages, overtime, shift differentials, stipends and other compensation in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Ensure proper withholding and deduction of taxes, benefits, garnishments, and other payroll-related deductions. Audit payroll registers and resolve discrepancies before final payroll submission. Maintain accurate payroll records and employee files while ensuring confidentiality of sensitive information. Assist with payroll tax reporting, year-end processing, annual audit, and preparation and distribution of W-2 forms. Reconcile payroll reports and support finance, as directed, with payroll-related journal entries and account reconciliations. Monitor compliance with federal, state, and local wage and hour regulations. Generate payroll reports for management, finance, and external auditors as needed. Coordinate with the Office of Human Resources regarding employee status changes, benefits administration Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7887aca0abfca001a0f3fc090871e7": {"title": "Digital Creator", "description": "Digital Creator.  Carlow University is now accepting applications for our Digital Creator role. The Digital Creator strengthens Carlow University's digital footprint through original, engaging storytelling across social media, web, email, and internal channels. This role captures authentic student experiences, campus life, academic programs, events, and institutional messages in ways that connect with prospective students, current students, faculty, staff, alumni, and community partners. This position helps bring Carlow's brand promise, \"Devoted to the Future of You,\" to life by highlighting what makes the university distinct: Mercy values, personal attention, Pittsburgh's Oakland location, and strong student outcomes. Key Responsibilities Digital Storytelling & Production Create multimedia material for social platforms, web, email, and internal use, including short-form video, photos, graphics, Stories, Reels, and posts Showcase student experience, academics, athletics, residence life, student support, and mission-driven initiatives Capture day-in-the-life and behind-the-scenes moments across campus, clinical placements, service projects, and Oakland Interview students, faculty, alumni, and staff to gather authentic stories and perspectives Translate Carlow's Mercy values of hospitality, service, discovery, and sacredness of creation into human-centered storytelling Optimize posts and digital assets for SEO, AEO, and platform best practices Social Media & Digital Platforms Plan, create, and schedule posts for Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, X, LinkedIn, YouTube, and internal digital platforms Support always-on storytelling and campaigns tied to the student journey and major university moments Monitor comments, messages, and tags, respond appropriately, and escalate when needed Experiment with trends, formats, and platform features to keep Carlow relevant and competitive Prioritize authentic, student-shot and lo-fi material when it supports stronger engagement Track performance metrics including reach, engagement, follower growth, video views, saves, shares, click-throughs, and traffic Use analytics to refine topics, formats, timing, and calls to action Student Experience & User-Generated Material Collaborate with student ambassadors, clubs, athletics, residence life, and other campus partners to source stories Curate and reshare student-generated posts, photos, and videos with proper permissions Attend campus events to capture real-time moments Build relationships with diverse student populations, including first-generation, transfer, adult, commuter, residential, traditional, and non-traditional students Brand Voice & Creative Development Help maintain Carlow's brand voice across channels: student-centered, mission-driven, and grounded in \"Devoted to the Future of You\" Ensure all work reflects Carlow's visual identity, accessibility standards, and brand guidelines Develop audience-specific storytelling for prospective students, adult learners, graduate students, alumni, donors, and community partners Build a creative style that feels authentic to Carlow and flexible across platforms Collaboration & Workflow Work closely with Marketing & Communications, Admissions, Advancement, Athletics, Academic Affairs, and Student Affairs Maintain a forward-looking calendar tied to enrollment cycles, campus events, and institutional priorities Organize and manage digital assets for efficient reuse Participate in team planning, brainstorms, and professional development Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Social Media, Digital Media, Graphic Design, or a related field, or equivalent experience Strong social media writing and editing skills across multiple audiences and platforms Portfolio required, with examples of original digital work across platforms Proficiency with tools such as: Short-form video editing tools Design platforms such as Canva, Adobe Express, or Adobe Creative Cloud Social media scheduling tools such as Sprout Understanding of current social media trends, platform behavior, and best practices Ability to create for digital signage and internal screens with concise messaging and strong visual hierarchy Ability to work on-site at Carlow's Oakland campus, including occasional evenings and weekends Preferred Qualifications Experience creating digital material in a mission-driven environment Familiarity with SEO and AEO best practices Experience as a student creator, ambassador, RA, or similar campus role Photography and videography experience Experience with CMS, email platforms, intranet systems, or digital signage systems Understanding of accessibility standards and ADA compliance Passion for human-centered storytelling Key Skills & Competencies Original, platform-native creative production Multimedia storytelling Brand voice development Curiosity and trend awareness Analytical thinking Audience insight Collaboration and relationship-building Organization and project management Accessibility-minded communication What Makes This Role Successful Growth in follower count, reach, engagement, video views, saves, shares, and profile visits Strong performance of social and digital storytelling across platforms Timely, accurate, and effective internal messaging Increased use of student voice and user-generated material Consistent alignment with Carlow's brand, mission, and accessibility standards Strong support of enrollment, advancement, and institutional priorities Meaningful interaction with prospective students, current students, alumni, and community members Carlow University is Devoted to.... A culture of integrity, dignity and respect for all A strong commitment to social justice Ethical forward-thinking leadership Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life & disability benefits package Tuition benefits for undergraduate and graduate programs Health Savings Account and Flexible Spending Account options Wellness and Employee Assistance Program Complimentary use of Carlow\u2019s fitness center and amenities Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859fa064222601a08d174c28636b": {"title": "Part-Time TRiO Assistive Technology Specialist", "description": "Part-Time TRiO Assistive Technology Specialist.  Funded by the U.S. Department of Education, Office of Postsecondary Education\u2019s Student Support Services Program, this part-time position will provide support services to students from low-income backgrounds, first-generation college students, and students with disabilities to increase their rates of retention, graduation, and persistence to graduation. The TRiO Assistive Technology Specialist is part of the instruction and support network for the Carlow SSS TRiO project and will design and facilitate workshops that enable students to learn and apply assistive technologies and digital literacy skills. Essential Functions Develop and instruct workshops and supplemental instruction regarding assistive technologies, including technologies available through University licenses as well as individual applications for use on student devices. Design and instruct student workshops and reviews focused on the use of various assistive technologies. Develop and maintain a caseload of SSS students who use assistive technologies, including meeting with students as needed and providing follow-up while working collaboratively with Disability Services Office (DSO) staff. Build and maintain a small caseload of approximately 30 students through facilitating workshops focused on self-management skills. Maintain student records in a confidential manner in accordance with FERPA and ADA requirements. Communicate with interested parties as needed and as appropriate. Create and update informational and instructional sheets and digital pages related to assistive technologies. Collaborate with the Information Technology (IT) Department and Procurement in the purchase and maintenance of software, web-based applications, and licenses. Research and assist with budgeting for new products for student use. Other Non-Essential Functions Attend meetings as scheduled and attend orientation events. Perform other related duties as required or assigned. Minimum Education Required Minimum: Bachelor\u2019s degree in instructional design, assistive technology, or a related field. Preferred: Master\u2019s degree in instructional design, assistive technology, or a related field. Related Experience Required The ideal candidate will: Have proven technology skills and possess a strong degree of comfort with hardware, software, and web-based applications. Be able to effectively problem-solve and handle potentially stressful situations with grace. Demonstrate strong attention to detail and the ability to follow directions. Possess outstanding written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrate the ability to be flexible in a changing environment. Be able to maintain appropriate boundaries while promoting independent learning and the transfer of skills. Interested applicants who have overcome similar barriers, including low income, being a first-generation college student, or having disabilities, are encouraged to apply. Required or Related Skills Ability to work a varied schedule with flexible hours, including some evening and occasional weekend hours; ability to act effectively in emergency and crisis situations. Familiarity with current trends in higher education and technology, and the ability to enhance the use of technology and other resources to meet student needs. Ability to build strong working alliances with students, staff, and faculty who may hold differing viewpoints. Ability to work collaboratively while always maintaining confidentiality and discretion. Must be capable of communicating with confidence and comfort and of sustaining individual and group social interactions in a variety of settings. Ability to establish a safe and respectful environment with individuals and in group settings. Detail-oriented with strong organizational skills. Student-service oriented and student-focused. Carlow University is a comprehensive Catholic University situated in a culturally rich and diverse urban setting of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1929 by the Sisters of Mercy, an international community of Roman Catholic women with a mission to serve the poor, the sick, and the uneducated. Carlow is an institution grounded in the liberal arts while also offering strong professional programs, committed to engaging its community in a process of life-long learning, scholarship, research, and service. Degrees are offered at the baccalaureate, master's, and doctoral levels. Carlow University aims to provide transformational educational opportunities rooted in social justice for a community of learners, and to empower them to excel in their chosen work as compassionate, responsible leaders in the creation of a just and merciful world. Carlow University employees commit themselves to the highest standards of ethical conduct. They commit to act with integrity, treat others with respect and dignity, carefully steward the University's resources, avoid conflicts of interest or commitment, maintain confidentiality, and to comply with legal and professional obligations. APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"}}, "rows": {"https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7883ac9e6b0bdf019e9456955e0ea4": {"school_id": 1196, "posting_url": "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a7883ac9e6b0bdf019e9456955e0ea4", "job_title_in_post": "Major Gifts Officer", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859f9fd3baa001a01c91ce7561e9": {"school_id": 1196, "posting_url": "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d061f94ddb0162022ae9e952fc&id=8a78859f9fd3baa001a01c91ce7561e9", "job_title_in_post": "Vice President for University Advancement and Alumni Engagement", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "October